<acknowledgement xml:id="acknowledgement">
    <title>Acknowledgements</title>

    <p>
      This textbook was made possible through the generous support of the 
      Community College of Rhode Island, which granted a sabbatical leave 
      providing the dedicated time needed to reimagine and author this 
      open-access curriculum for our introductory computer science students. 
      I am deeply grateful to the sabbatical review committee, 
	  my chairperson and colleagues in the Department of Computer 
      Science &amp; Cybersecurity, and my colleagues across CCRI for their encouragement, 
      insightful discussions, and shared commitment to accessible computer 
      science education.
    </p>

    <p>
      Special thanks go to the many generations of CCRI students whose curiosity, 
      thoughtful questions, and honest feedback in the classroom have continually 
      shaped how these programming concepts are explained, visualized, and scaffolded.
	  You inspire me daily with your drive and resilience, and it is an honor to teach and learn alongside you.
    </p>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Note on AI-Assisted Authoring</title>
      <p>
        In the development of this textbook, generative artificial intelligence 
        tools were used collaboratively as an authoring assistant, research partner, 
        and for technical production. Generative tools assisted with structuring 
        exercises, drafting some initial scenario narratives, critiquing the author's narratives,
		generating PreTeXt XML mark-up, 
        and rendering call stack memory models and structure charts. 
        All pedagogy, curricular sequencing, code examples, technical explanations, 
        and solutions were designed, directed, verified, and edited by the author, 
        who retains sole responsibility for the content and educational integrity of 
        this work.
      </p>
    </paragraphs>
  </acknowledgement>

